            _t("API requests", "A script can send an HTTP request and print the status and body. Use the authorised test URL from the lab. Treat the response as data, not as instructions to run."),
            _t("Regular expressions", "A regular expression is a pattern for matching text, such as 'a word made of digits'. They are useful for finding an address in a log line. A pattern that is too loose matches the wrong lines."),
            _t("Bash", "Bash is a command language on Linux. A script is a text file of commands you could have typed. Start with variables and if. Run bash scripts only in the lab account."),
            _t("PowerShell", "PowerShell is a command language on Windows. Commands are often Verb-Noun, such as Get-Process. It can administer the computer, so a copied script can do more than you meant. Read it before you run it."),
