            _t("C programming introduction", "C is a language close to the machine. You will see it later in system software. For now, know that a C program is compiled into a file the computer runs, and that memory mistakes in C are a historic source of serious flaws."),
            _t("Algorithms", "An algorithm is a finite list of steps that solves a class of problems. Sorting names alphabetically is an algorithm. The steps must be clear enough that a computer, or another person, can follow them."),
            _t("Data structures", "A data structure is a way of organising values, such as a list, a dictionary, or a tree. The choice changes how fast a program can find something. At this stage, lists and dictionaries are enough."),
