            _t("Why cybersecurity exists", "People store money, identity, health, and work on computers. Those systems fail from mistakes, crime, and accidents. The field exists because the damage is real and the systems are shared."),
            _t("Information security and cybersecurity", "Information security protects information in any form, including paper. Cybersecurity focuses on electronic systems. A locked filing cabinet is information security. A locked account is both."),
            _t("Confidentiality", "Confidentiality means only the people who should see information can see it. Encryption and access control are common ways to support it."),
            _t("Integrity", "Integrity means information has not been changed without authorisation, and that you can detect a change. A checksum or a signature is a tool for that check."),
            _t("Availability", "Availability means the system works when it is needed. A backup and a spare path support availability. A system that is perfectly secret but always offline has failed this goal."),
